WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Instructor] Our
squirrel friend here likes

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.960
to collect acorns, because, really,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.430
that's how he is able to live.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:11.430
And let's say everyday, he
collects exactly three acorns.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.660
And so what I'm curious
about is how many acorns

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.170
will he have after doing
this for five days?

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.400
So one way to think about
it is every day he is able

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.690
to collect a group of three acorns.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.210
So you could view this
as maybe what he's able

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.250
to collect in day one.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.310
And then in day two, he's
able to collect a second group

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.610
of three acorns.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.260
In day three, he's able
to collect another group

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.420
of three acorns.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.790
And every day it's a
equal number of acorns

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:40.623
that he's collecting.

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:42.450
On the fourth day, another three.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.920
On the fifth day, another three.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.800
And so if you were curious
how many total acorns

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.630
he's collected, well, you
could just count them up,

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.410
or you could think about,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:57.160
well, he's got five
groups of three acorns.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.510
Five equal groups of three acorns.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.200
So you could say five groups

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.510
of three acorns, three acorns.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.800
And so the total amount would be five,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.283
we could view this as five threes.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.550
Now, five threes, you could view this

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.500
as five threes added together.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.020
Three plus three, plus three,
plus three, plus three.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.370
And if you wanted to calculate this,

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.610
you could skip count by three.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.270
So this would be three, six, nine, 12, 15,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.770
because we add three, we get to six,

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.000
we add another three, we get to nine,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.300
we add another three, we get to 12,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.140
we add another three, we get to 15.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.860
And so this would be a way of recognizing

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.740
that you have 15 acorns,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.570
but we're starting to touch
on one of the most fundamental

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.960
ideas in all of mathematics.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.390
In fact, we actually are applying it,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.950
we just haven't used the world,

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.440
and that's, we are multiplying.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.373
We are using multiplication.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.280
All multiplication is

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:09.280
is this notion of multiple
equal groups of something.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.680
So, here, one way to
express what we just did,

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.230
is we just, when we said five threes,

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.940
that's the same thing as five,

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.420
and I'm going to introduce
a new symbol to you,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.203
five times three.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.590
So all of these things are equivalent.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.860
You're already used to seeing equal groups

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.400
and multiple equal groups,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.590
and you're used to adding
something multiple times,

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.140
and you're used to skip counting,

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.240
and all of that is, in
some way shape or form,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.920
you have been doing multiplication.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.520
So when someone says five times three,

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.130
you could view that is
five groups of three,

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.790
or you could view that as five threes,

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:51.990
or you could view that
as three plus three,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.070
plus three, plus three,

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.910
or you could view that as 15.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.280
I'll leave ya there.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.020
There's a lot of practice on Khan Academy

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:01.853
to work through this

00:03:01.853 --> 00:03:04.830
and make sure you get the underlying idea.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.880
But as you'll see, this is
perhaps one of the most useful

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.563
concepts that you might
learn in your entire lives.

